<article class="env-example" id="02PR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02PR">Example <span data-tag="02PR">42.68.21</span>.</a> Let $R = k$ be a field. Let $M = k^{\oplus a} \oplus k^{\oplus b}$ be $l = a + b$ dimensional. Let $\varphi $ and $\psi $ be the following diagonal matrices </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \varphi = \text{diag}(u_1, \ldots , u_ a, 0, \ldots , 0), \quad \psi = \text{diag}(0, \ldots , 0, v_1, \ldots , v_ b)  \]
</div>
  <p> with $u_ i, v_ j \in k^*$. In this case we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \det \nolimits _ k(M, \varphi , \psi ) = \frac{u_1 \ldots u_ a}{v_1 \ldots v_ b}.  \]
</div>
  <p> This can be seen by a direct computation or by computing in case $l = 1$ and using the additivity of Lemma <a href="/tag/02PO" data-tag="02PO">42.68.18</a>. </p>
</article>